---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import GuideLink from "../../components/GuideLink.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Enshrouded 1.0 Skill Tree Reset: New Skills and What to Re-Spend"
  description="Enshrouded 1.0 resets every skill tree and adds 8 new skills — Advanced Necromancy, Totem Mastery and Blast and Cast for mages, Puncture, Barrage and Survival Instinct for archers."
>
  <p><span class="tag">Enshrouded 1.0</span> <span class="tag">Skills</span> <span class="tag">Last verified 2026-10-14</span></p>
  <h1>Enshrouded 1.0 Skill Tree Reset: New Skills and What to Re-Spend</h1>

  <p class="muted">
    <strong>Enshrouded 1.0 resets your skill tree.</strong> Skills were both added and moved around, so
    Keen Games refunds your points and asks you to re-spend them — and they have said this should be the
    last reset. Re-assign your points <em>before you leave your base</em> on launch day, together with
    the level cap rising to 50 and gear to level 55.
  </p>

  <div class="toc">
    <strong>On this page</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#reset">Why the tree resets and what to do</a></li>
      <li><a href="#new-skills">The 8 new skills</a></li>
      <li><a href="#caps">New level and gear caps</a></li>
      <li><a href="#spend">How to spend your points</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="reset">Why the tree resets and what to do</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      The reset is not a punishment — it is a consequence of the tree changing shape. New nodes were
      added (the two summon nodes plus new wand attacks) and existing skills were moved, so old builds
      cannot map cleanly onto the new tree. Keen Games refunds the points and lets you rebuild.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      <strong>Practical order of operations on launch day:</strong> load in, stay at your base, open the
      skill tree, and spend the points before you head into a fight. Leaving your base with an empty or
      half-built tree is the single most common way to have a bad first hour.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="new-skills">The 8 new skills</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Skill</th><th>Class</th><th>Effect</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Advanced Necromancy</td><td>Mage</td><td>Increases your skeleton summon limit — the core node for a necromancer build.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Totem Mastery</td><td>Mage</td><td>Increases your totem summon limit — the core node for a totem build.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Blast and Cast</td><td>Mage</td><td>After a wand critical hit, increases your next staff attack's base damage by 50% within 10 seconds. Rewards switching weapons mid-fight.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Aerial Wand Attack</td><td>Mage</td><td>Enables a mid-air wand attack with area damage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wand Evasion Attack</td><td>Mage</td><td>Enables a wider piercing wand projectile paired with a backward hop.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Puncture</td><td>Archer</td><td>Increases ranged piercing damage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Barrage</td><td>Archer</td><td>Chance to restore bow durability on hits — a sustain node for long fights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Survival Instinct</td><td>Archer</td><td>Killing Shroud-infested enemies with a bow or dagger adds time in the Shroud.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="muted">
    Note the pattern: five of the eight are mage nodes. 1.0 deliberately targets magic, which had the
    narrowest options in Early Access.
  </p>

  <h2 id="caps">New level and gear caps</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Cap</th><th>Before</th><th>With 1.0</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Player level</td><td>Lower Early Access cap</td><td><strong>50</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Equipment level</td><td>Lower Early Access cap</td><td><strong>55</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The new caps arrive alongside the new <strong>Cinder's Cradle</strong> biome and new enemy
    variants across all factions, including <strong>heavy and elite</strong> versions — 37 new enemy
    types and variants in total. In other words, the ceiling goes up because the content got harder, not
    only because the numbers grew.
  </p>

  <h2 id="spend">How to spend your points</h2>
  <p>
    These are directions rather than fixed builds — with points refunded, the cost of trying a new
    archetype at 1.0 is zero.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">Solo play</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">
        Summons carry solo runs because they give you bodies to hold enemies while you reposition.
        Advanced Necromancy and Totem Mastery increase how many you can keep active, which is more
        valuable early than stacking damage passives.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">Groups and crowds</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">
        Blizzard and Ball Lightning are the new area-damage options. If you fight packs rather than
        single targets, these two plus the rebalance are the fastest upgrade to your clear speed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">Tough single targets</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">
        Open with Entangle to hold the target, then land a wand critical and follow with a staff attack
        to trigger Blast and Cast. It is the skill designed around weapon swapping.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">Long fights</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">
        Mana Drain plus reduced-mana-cost perks on Eternal spells keeps you casting instead of waiting
        on regeneration.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p><strong>Does Enshrouded 1.0 reset the skill tree?</strong><br />Yes. Skills were added and moved, so the tree resets and your points are refunded for re-spending. Keen Games has described it as hopefully the last reset.</p>
    <p><strong>Do I lose my points permanently?</strong><br />No — they are refunded. You re-spend them in the tree.</p>
    <p><strong>When should I respec?</strong><br />Immediately after loading 1.0, before leaving your base.</p>
    <p><strong>What is the new level cap?</strong><br />Player level 50, equipment level 55.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>How many new skills are there?</strong><br />Eight: five mage skills and three archer skills.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Related 1.0 guides</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-3">
    <GuideLink title="1.0 Release Overview" desc="Date, platforms, price, level cap and every confirmed change in one place." href="/guides/enshrouded-1-0-release/" badge="1.0" />
    <GuideLink title="New Spells in 1.0" desc="All 9 new spells, the summons category and 22 tier-7 Eternal versions." href="/guides/enshrouded-1-0-new-spells/" badge="1.0" />
    <GuideLink title="Sparkworks Guide" desc="Levers, pressure plates and logic gates — build your own dungeon." href="/guides/enshrouded-1-0-sparkworks/" badge="1.0" />
  </div>

  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:0.85rem">
    Source: Keen Games' official pre-launch material and the 1.0 launch trailer. Build suggestions
    are our own, based on the confirmed skill effects. Keen's full release changelog, due on launch day,
    may still adjust individual skill numbers.
  </p>
</Base>
